ed or ended. He was alone with his thoughts and the unending stream of people who went by each second but who somehow seemed to disappear before they could truly begin their own", "text_sha256": "c18aaf152dd6c24f9c4bdb7b6c5b8c46f8be585afea0923ae0aa41e569ce9591", "token_ids": [23705, 279, 2526, 39579, 22152, 539, 13876, 314, 1016, 19447, 59842, 321, 20078, 8796, 314, 49483, 59731, 286, 383, 13280, 62530, 12965, 1172, 279, 12967, 3000, 10729, 3808, 279, 21664, 12269, 13, 561, 3594, 557, 11702, 440, 279, 39029, 314, 51764, 10482, 26034, 321, 56540, 77591, 51432, 494, 264, 1898, 2250, 888, 303, 279, 8858, 13, 357, 6103, 12967, 25035, 557, 303, 4936, 13, 3648, 855, 42578, 8097, 391, 506, 279, 19695, 15589, 494, 780, 49755, 1345, 780, 7168, 14466, 54166, 383, 279, 809, 314, 279, 4392, 383, 780, 22682, 26, 1292, 8632, 1132, 264, 2342, 29636, 430, 551, 8308, 310, 8307, 279, 86088, 49093, 4732, 13, 1049, 557, 3999, 310, 12426, 1092, 836, 19451, 995, 978, 3604, 2394, 1483, 3603, 948, 279, 18146, 3727, 32874, 430, 9163, 18716, 279, 51172, 4661, 836, 7808, 13, 561, 20513, 557, 8545, 3213, 310, 3379, 685, 2272, 279, 14979, 12681, 314, 836, 37260, 53768, 430, 781, 28260, 364, 279, 5647, 13, 39792, 279, 3136, 781, 5312, 59384, 34294, 680, 314, 264, 20857, 421, 874, 10179, 6749, 1040, 424, 995, 978, 1801, 303, 264, 3980, 303, 4357, 524, 1248, 3998, 27090, 35916, 8464, 25082, 303, 4184, 579, 27786, 6213, 321, 279, 1560, 279, 12967, 3000, 4062, 279, 21664, 12269, 303, 1248, 28945, 314, 6414, 13, 3984, 9047, 310, 10602, 23221, 279, 39579, 6171, 579, 3609, 430, 551, 9770, 780, 3609, 18253, 1973, 3397, 8306, 424, 310, 2873, 449, 10429, 14996, 314, 948, 279, 1834, 995, 3404, 3727, 466, 9202, 13, 1216, 557, 7249, 440, 780, 10976, 321, 279, 632, 2379, 4129, 314, 1208, 852, 3804, 539, 1754, 2018, 694, 852, 16429, 9047, 310, 30035, 1518, 781, 1362, 9149, 3060, 836, 1765], "packet_bytes": 104, "tokens": 277, "packet_tokens": 277, "encode_seconds": 30.682254866929725, "decode_seconds": 42.771164749981835, "net_bpt": 0.4620938628158845, "gross_bpt": 3.003610108303249, "attempts_used": 1, "keyless_probe": {"0": {"status": "zero_width_interval", "tokens_observed": 169}, "128": {"status": "admissible", "tokens_observed": 169}}, "natural": {"mode": "matched_q_sampler", "status": "complete", "error": null, "cover_text": "Inside the small cafe the afternoon light fell across the wooden tables. Dust motes danced rhythmically in the shafts of golden light that sliced through the tall windows like silver rivers. Outside the single-pane glass of the small window above the seating area could be seen the distant silhouette of a street vendor strolling with his tray slung over his shoulder—nothing new to those who knew the rhythms of the neighborhood long enough to notice. The air was heavy with the scent of roasted bread and stale cigarette ash from the barista who had just broken pointlessly late. It was a place where time seemed to hang suspended between the hum of the nearby bus and the quiet murmur of a story that was just beginning. Patrons shuffled casually across the worn wood legs of the bar stools; an elderly couple murmured lowly about politics while another woman carefully folded a napkin before pocketing it. Despite the stillness of the interior and the slow pace of the timepiece in the corner fixture on the bar—clock ticking only once a second or twice—a profound stillness held the room. The only sound was the soft clinking of cups against saucers and the rustle of someone turning a page in a battered history book. Here in this space of quietude against the noise of the day outside was captured in the amber haze of late afternoon light. As the clock on the coffee", "token_ids": [23705, 279, 2526, 39579, 279, 12967, 3000, 10729, 3808, 279, 21664, 12269, 13, 30939, 3724, 287, 80863, 35091, 2586, 303, 279, 29379, 82, 314, 20117, 3000, 421, 46028, 1472, 279, 15740, 10708, 1040, 14527, 34343, 13, 39792, 279, 3074, 37175, 8720, 314, 279, 2526, 3136, 3294, 279,